msgid "llvm-profdata - Profile data tool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:6
#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:29
#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:283
#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:400
#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:462
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:8
msgid "{program}`llvm-profdata` *command* \\[*args...*\\]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:10
#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:33
#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:287
#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:404
#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:466
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:12
msgid ""
"The {program}`llvm-profdata` tool is a small utility for working with "
"profile data files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:15
msgid "COMMANDS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:17
msgid "{ref}`merge <profdata-merge>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:18
msgid "{ref}`show <profdata-show>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:19
msgid "{ref}`overlap <profdata-overlap>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:20
msgid "{ref}`order <profdata-order>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:27
msgid "MERGE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:31
msgid "{program}`llvm-profdata merge` \\[*options*\\] \\[*filename...*\\]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:35
msgid ""
"{program}`llvm-profdata merge` takes several profile data files generated by "
"PGO instrumentation and merges them together into a single indexed profile "
"data file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:39
msgid ""
"By default profile data is merged without modification. This means that the "
"relative importance of each input file is proportional to the number of "
"samples or counts it contains. In general, the input from a longer training "
"run will be interpreted as relatively more important than a shorter run. "
"Depending on the nature of the training runs it may be useful to adjust the "
"weight given to each input file by using the `-weighted-input` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:46
msgid ""
"Profiles passed in via `-weighted-input`, `-input-files`, or via positional "
"arguments are processed once for each time they are seen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:49
#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:296
#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:430
#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:475
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:52
#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:319
#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:437
#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:478
msgid "Print a summary of command line options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:56
msgid ""
"Specify the output file name. *Output* cannot be `-` as the resulting "
"indexed profile data can't be written to standard output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:61
msgid ""
"Specify an input file name along with a weight. The profile counts of the "
"supplied `filename` will be scaled (multiplied) by the supplied `weight`, "
"where `weight` is a decimal integer >= 1. Input files specified without "
"using this option are assigned a default weight of 1. Examples are shown "
"below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:69
msgid ""
"Specify a file which contains a list of files to merge. The entries in this "
"file are newline-separated. Lines starting with '#' are skipped. Entries may "
"be of the form \\<filename> or \\<weight>,\\<filename>."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:75
msgid ""
"Specify a file which contains a remapping from symbol names in the input "
"profile to the symbol names that should be used in the output profile. The "
"file should consist of lines of the form `<input-symbol> <output-symbol>`. "
"Blank lines and lines starting with `#` are skipped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:80
msgid ""
"The {doc}`llvm-cxxmap <llvm-cxxmap>` tool can be used to generate the symbol "
"remapping file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:85
#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:328
msgid "Specify that the input profile is an instrumentation-based profile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:89
#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:345
msgid "Specify that the input profile is a sample-based profile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:91
msgid "The format of the generated file can be generated in one of three ways:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:96
msgid ""
"Emit the profile using a binary encoding. For instrumentation-based profile "
"the output format is the indexed binary format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:102
msgid ""
"Emit the profile using an extensible binary encoding. This option can only "
"be used with sample-based profile. The extensible binary encoding can be "
"more compact with compression enabled and can be loaded faster than the "
"default binary encoding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:110
msgid ""
"Emit the profile in text mode. This option can also be used with both sample-"
"based and instrumentation-based profile. When this option is used the "
"profile will be dumped in the text format that is parsable by the profile "
"reader."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:118
msgid "Emit the profile using GCC's gcov format (Not yet supported)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:122
msgid ""
"Do not emit function records with 0 execution count. Can only be used in "
"conjunction with -instr. Defaults to false, since it can inhibit compiler "
"optimization during PGO."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:128
msgid ""
"Use N threads to perform profile merging. When N=0, llvm-profdata auto-"
"detects an appropriate number of threads to use. This is the default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:133
msgid ""
"Set the failure mode. There are two options: 'any' causes the merge command "
"to fail if any profiles are invalid, and 'all' causes the merge command to "
"fail only if all profiles are invalid. If 'all' is set, information from any "
"invalid profiles is excluded from the final merged product. The default "
"failure mode is 'any'."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:141
msgid ""
"Specify a file which contains a list of symbols to generate profile symbol "
"list in the profile. This option can only be used with sample-based profile "
"in extbinary format. The entries in this file are newline-separated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:147
msgid ""
"Compress all sections when writing the profile. This option can only be used "
"with sample-based profile in extbinary format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:152
msgid ""
"Use MD5 to represent string in name table when writing the profile. This "
"option can only be used with sample-based profile in extbinary format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:157
msgid ""
"Mark the profile to be a partial profile which only provides partial profile "
"coverage for the optimized target. This option can only be used with sample-"
"based profile in extbinary format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:163
msgid ""
"Split the profile data section to two with one containing sample profiles "
"with inlined functions and the other not. This option can only be used with "
"sample-based profile in extbinary format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:169
msgid ""
"Convert the merged profile into a profile with a new layout. Supported "
"layout are `nest` (Nested profile, the input should be CS flat profile) and "
"`flat` (Profile with nested inlinees flattened out)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:175
msgid ""
"Supplement an instrumentation profile with sample profile. The sample "
"profile is the input of the flag. Output will be in instrumentation format "
"(only works with -instr)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:181
msgid ""
"For the function which is cold in instr profile but hot in sample profile, "
"if the ratio of the number of zero counters divided by the total number of "
"counters is above the threshold, the profile of the function will be "
"regarded as being harmful for performance and will be dropped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:188
msgid ""
"User specified cold threshold for instr profile which will override the cold "
"threshold got from profile summary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:193
msgid ""
"If the size of a function is smaller than the threshold, assume it can be "
"inlined by PGO early inliner and it will not be adjusted based on sample "
"profile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:199
msgid ""
"Specify the executable or `.dSYM` that contains debug info for the raw "
"profile. When `--debug-info-correlate` or `--profile-correlate=debug-info` "
"was used for instrumentation, use this option to correlate the raw profile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:205
msgid ""
"Specify the executable that contains profile data and profile name sections "
"for the raw profile. When `-profile-correlate=binary` was used for "
"instrumentation, use this option to correlate the raw profile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:211
msgid ""
"Use debuginfod to find the associated executables that contain profile data "
"and name sections for the raw profiles to correlate them. When -profile-"
"correlate=binary was used for instrumentation, this option can be used for "
"correlation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:218
msgid ""
"Use provided local directories to search for executables that contain "
"profile data and name sections for the raw profiles to correlate them. When -"
"profile-correlate=binary was used for instrumentation, this option can be "
"used for correlation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:225
msgid ""
"Specify the correlation kind (debug_info or binary) to use when -debuginfod "
"or -debug-file-directory=\\<dir> option is provided."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:230
msgid ""
"The maximum number of temporal profile traces to be stored in the output "
"profile. If more traces are added, we will use reservoir sampling to select "
"which traces to keep. Note that changing this value between different merge "
"invocations on the same indexed profile could result in sample bias. The "
"default value is 100."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:238
msgid ""
"The maximum number of functions in a single temporal profile trace. Longer "
"traces will be truncated. The default value is 1000."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:243
msgid ""
"Only keep functions matching the regex in the output, all others are erased "
"from the profile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:248
msgid ""
"Remove functions matching the regex from the profile. If both --function and "
"--no-function are specified and a function matches both, it is removed."
msgstr ""

