#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:281
msgid "SHOW"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:285
msgid "{program}`llvm-profdata show` \\[*options*\\] \\[*filename*\\]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:289
msgid ""
"{program}`llvm-profdata show` takes a profile data file and displays the "
"information about the profile counters for this file and for any of the "
"specified function(s)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:293
msgid ""
"If *filename* is omitted or is `-`, then **llvm-profdata show** reads its "
"input from standard input."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:299
msgid "Print details for every function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:303
msgid "Print embedded binary ids in a profile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:307
msgid "Print the counter values for the displayed functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:311
msgid ""
"Emit output in the selected format if supported by the provided profile type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:315
#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:433
msgid ""
"Print details for a function if the function's name contains the given "
"string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:323
#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:441
#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:482
msgid ""
"Specify the output file name. If *output* is `-` or it isn't specified, then "
"the output is sent to standard output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:332
msgid ""
"Instruct the profile dumper to show profile counts in the text format of the "
"instrumentation-based profile data representation. By default, the profile "
"information is dumped in a more human-readable form (also in text) with "
"annotations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:339
msgid ""
"Instruct the profile dumper to show the top `n` functions with the hottest "
"basic blocks in the summary section. By default, the topn functions are not "
"dumped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:349
msgid ""
"Show the profiled sizes of the memory intrinsic calls for shown functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:353
msgid ""
"Show only those functions whose max count values are greater or equal to "
"`n`. By default, the value-cutoff is set to 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:358
msgid ""
"Only output names of functions whose max count value are below the cutoff "
"value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:363
msgid "Print profile version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:367
msgid ""
"Only show context sensitive profile counts. The default is to filter all "
"context sensitive profile counts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:372
msgid ""
"Show profile symbol list if it exists in the profile. This option is only "
"meaningful for sample-based profile in extbinary format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:377
msgid ""
"Show basic information about each section in the profile. This option is "
"only meaningful for sample-based profile in extbinary format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:382
msgid ""
"Specify the executable or `.dSYM` that contains debug info for the raw "
"profile. When `--debug-info-correlate` or `--profile-correlate=debug-info` "
"was used for instrumentation, use this option to show the correlated "
"functions from the raw profile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:389
msgid ""
"Show only the functions that have been executed, i.e., functions with non-"
"zero counts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:398
msgid "OVERLAP"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:402
msgid ""
"{program}`llvm-profdata overlap` \\[*options*\\] \\[*base profile file*\\] "
"\\[*test profile file*\\]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:406
msgid ""
"{program}`llvm-profdata overlap` takes two profile data files and displays "
"the *overlap* of counter distribution between the whole files and between "
"any of the specified functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:410
msgid ""
"In this command, *overlap* is defined as follows: Suppose *base profile "
"file* has the following counts: {c1_1, c1_2, ..., c1_n, c1_u_1, c2_u_2, ..., "
"c2_u_s}, and *test profile file* has {c2_1, c2_2, ..., c2_n, c2_v_1, "
"c2_v_2, ..., c2_v_t}. Here c{1|2}\\_i (i = 1 .. n) are matched counters and "
"c1_u_i (i = 1 .. s) and c2_v_i (i = 1 .. v) are unmatched counters (or "
"counters only existing in) *base profile file* and *test profile file*, "
"respectively. Let sum_1 = c1_1 + c1_2 + ... + c1_n + c1_u_1 + c2_u_2 + ... + "
"c2_u_s, and sum_2 = c2_1 + c2_2 + ... + c2_n + c2_v_1 + c2_v_2 + ... + "
"c2_v_t. *overlap* = min(c1_1/sum_1, c2_1/sum_2) + min(c1_2/sum_1, c2_2/"
"sum_2) + ... \\+ min(c1_n/sum_1, c2_n/sum_2)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:423
msgid ""
"The result overlap distribution is a percentage number, ranging from 0.0% to "
"100.0%, where 0.0% means there is no overlap and 100.0% means a perfect "
"overlap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:427
msgid ""
"Here is an example, if *base profile file* has counts of {400, 600}, and "
"*test profile file* has matched counts of {60000, 40000}. The *overlap* is "
"80%."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:446
msgid ""
"Show only those functions whose max count values are greater or equal to "
"`n`. By default, the value-cutoff is set to max of unsigned long long."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:451
msgid ""
"Only show overlap for the context sensitive profile counts. The default is "
"to show non-context sensitive profile counts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:460
msgid "ORDER"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:464
msgid "{program}`llvm-profdata order` \\[*options*\\] \\[*filename*\\]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:468
msgid ""
"{program}`llvm-profdata order` uses temporal profiling traces from a profile "
"and finds a function order that reduces the number of page faults for those "
"traces. This output can be directly passed to `lld` via `--symbol-ordering-"
"file=` for ELF or `-order-file` for Mach-O. If the traces found in the "
"profile are representative of the real world, then this order should improve "
"startup performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:486
msgid "EXIT STATUS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../CommandGuide/llvm-profdata.md:488
msgid ""
"{program}`llvm-profdata` returns 1 if the command is omitted or is invalid, "
"if it cannot read input files, or if there is a mismatch between their data."
msgstr ""
